The Nolan 'Dark Knight' Trilogy (and this film in particular) are truest to the comic book Batman character from the Golden Era of comics. 'Detective Comics' and 'Batman' were dark and gritty adult storylines. Batman is a human, with 'superpowers' of intellect, wealth, and discipline - Christian Bale plays the Batman character as it was originally meant to be played. Bale is more athletic than Keaton, more masculine and edgy than Clooney, more violent than Kilmer, and this version of Batman/Bruce Wayne was the first to have real depth.

In the 2020's, most people watch big-budget Marvel movies and think Marvel has won the comic book battle with DC. Marvel has literal armies of superheros and the deep pockets of Disney to support them. But, Marvel doesn't have The Batman. And, Marvel didn't make the greatest superhero adaptation of all time.

Real Review Posting Scoring Criteria:

Acting - 1/1;

Casting - 1/1;

Directing - 1/1;

Story - 1/1;

Writing/Screenplay - 1/1;

Total Base Score = 5

Modifiers (+ or -):

Cinematography: +1 (Most modern comic films rely too heavily on computer graphics. This film uses camera work to establish the pace of the action scenes and it feels more real.);

Standout Performances: +2 ( Christian Bale & Heath Ledger)l

Believability/Consistency: +1 ( This is one of the most believable 'Superhero' film adaptations.);

Quotability: +0.5 ( Heath Ledger's Joker is a cultural icon);

Ensemble Cast: +1;

Exceptional Choreography: +0.5 ( The fight scenes and stunts maintain the feel of realism.);

Total Real Review Rating: 10+

This film proves that superhero movies don't need to be about spandex costumes and Witty catchphrases, in fact to call this a superhero film would be an understatement, Christopher Nolan's directing has to be some of the greatest work I have ever seen, any movie he makes is guaranteed to be on the 250 highest rated movies on IMDB, inception the dark knight trilogy, etc. So let's talk about it;

Let's start with the plot, This has to be the best written superhero movie of all time, the dialogue is clever, it's just the right amount of disturbing and Christian bales performance in this film is underrated, sure Heath Ledgers performance makes his look like a twilight film but he delivered a really solid performance. The plot deals with the subject of staying noble while the joker tries to get him to reveal himself to the public, whilst threatening to kill people or blow up a hospital, this is easily the greatest film that I have ever seen. Another thing about the plot is the epic chase scene. It is perfectly shot, and goes on for just the right amount of time.

In conclusion a 9.0/10 won't make the cut for this. It should at least be a 9.8/10. As it is just my personal favourite and not the one that I think is the BEST.
